    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "tutor",
        "speaker": "Tutor",
        "sourceStart": 7,
        "sourceEnd": 81,
        "text": "Your interview guide seems to assume that the new study room is a success.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "742c0071c6d2200728f4e38ffc47208774fd35a4bf9d154f6a67a03814c8ae90",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 87,
        "sourceEnd": 214,
        "text": "My first question asks what users like most about it. I see the problem: it gives them no obvious route to say they dislike it.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "8ce18497c7e8f2a514d50697a2281d44b27627d570e91474d737872d7a7ddfa7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tutor",
        "speaker": "Tutor",
        "sourceStart": 222,
        "sourceEnd": 317,
        "text": "Try an open question about their experience before asking for a positive or negative judgement.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "23e5ed9f15c4849baecb6a2d91f42c5293629c5118e24ecfab16db1e540682a3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 323,
        "sourceEnd": 424,
        "text": "I will ask them to describe their most recent visit. Then I can ask what helped or caused difficulty.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "fa0ba7d571c3fff49f75ac1f46b2dab1f1a1b16167e0240dec8360dab830890b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tutor",
        "speaker": "Tutor",
        "sourceStart": 432,
        "sourceEnd": 465,
        "text": "How will you select participants?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "6bede6ce89dc4d972fea81b176e06f8723d1e6a2dab831a886614e5e80e9fd09",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 471,
        "sourceEnd": 639,
        "text": "Twelve interviews, including people who booked but did not attend. I can contact them through the booking office without receiving their private contact details myself.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "c9cfe14d99bf127b7a0fcc6f38a098fc536a26f4094d0370efe5c760b7592799",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tutor",
        "speaker": "Tutor",
        "sourceStart": 647,
        "sourceEnd": 668,
        "text": "What about recording?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "e06053bd833f21d516e271e121f76d587d8b4eef14f4023948b95f0f7185f9f1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 674,
        "sourceEnd": 775,
        "text": "I will request permission first. Anyone who declines can still take part, with written notes instead.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "722113401dd49a569c50480c8a8ccf2102794cd0315b670871159d07d5956f79",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tutor",
        "speaker": "Tutor",
        "sourceStart": 783,
        "sourceEnd": 823,
        "text": "Will you send participants your summary?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "33df40a8f1de2bb45ea30a3df5afbb39af77e54a9d1505b9355da2513d9aab3a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 829,
        "sourceEnd": 985,
        "text": "Yes, but I will distinguish a correction to what they said from a disagreement with my interpretation. Both may need recording; they are not the same issue.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "d29526b11746b48fea33fb797772301b08897a71ccd2ed2731ad9187e8d6d36b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tutor",
        "speaker": "Tutor",
        "sourceStart": 993,
        "sourceEnd": 1036,
        "text": "How will you handle contradictory accounts?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ec50e3371f6772bfe6bec017e817c31989cf6f8e67cb4e156b7ef8a27c2633e8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 1042,
        "sourceEnd": 1207,
        "text": "Keep them. One student may value the quiet while another finds the rules too restrictive. I should describe the difference rather than make everyone sound satisfied.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "e3cb9d4e82fc3adc2abec6408585f47bebf005d1dd13e24d7a79303b2e945523",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tutor",
        "speaker": "Tutor",
        "sourceStart": 1215,
        "sourceEnd": 1339,
        "text": "Good. Pilot the guide on Monday. The interviews can begin after we have checked that the wording does not steer the answers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ac8a22af3c2359614bc2c140bfe76a75c2d6cdadf927e052da9b195b229d08db",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
